WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.560
The review exercise aimed to get some essential&nbsp;
practice in documenting code. The assignment was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:11.400
to write documentation explaining what this code&nbsp;
does and then print it on the screen when it runs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.920
To accomplish this task, we need a docstring,&nbsp;
which can be added anywhere to the code. I will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:24.120
add the docstring above the current code, using&nbsp;
triple quotation marks for the docstring. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:32.720
to print the documentation out as part of the&nbsp;
output, I will add, to line 12, a print statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:45.000
that prints the docstrings, indicated by a double&nbsp;
underscore, doc, and another double underscore. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.640
will run this code, and we see the game results&nbsp;
and the docstring at the end of the results.

